The potential vulnerability is related to improper handling of file uploads, which can lead to a Remote Code Execution (RCE) vulnerability. This vulnerability arises when the application accepts files from users without adequately validating or restricting the types of files that can be uploaded. If the API allows the upload of arbitrary files, an attacker could upload a malicious file that, when processed by the server, could execute harmful code or scripts. The lack of stringent checks on the file type and content can result in the server executing unintended commands, thereby compromising the security of the application and the underlying system.

